From c316526c1cbd772a77a0e920867d0a4c51baf5d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 17:15:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 110/206] feat(shorebird): land --dump_object_pool and
 --dump_object_pool_link_data

Both flags are registered in their analyze_snapshot -- established
behaviourally, since `strings` cannot answer that question (--sdk_version is
registered and has no bare-name string either). --dump_object_pool_link_data is
a string option carrying its own path and needing no --out;
--dump_object_pool is a bool that writes to --out.

The producer is their GetObjectPoolLinkInfo (0x10024cb9c), and it has three
parts:

  * self_pp_indices / subgraph_pp_indices are the pool references the subgraph
    walk makes, in order and WITH REPEATS. All 1380 of each on their own
    base.so; deduplicating drops to 1250/932.

  * `pairs` is not a code scan. Shorebird narrowed EntryType to two bits at
    position 2 and put a two-bit PairPosition at 0..1 of the object pool's
    entry_bits, and GetObjectPoolLinkInfo reports every index marked
    kPairFirst. The layout is confirmed three ways and the values come from the
    literal entry_bits their own code stores (0x09, 0x05/0x65, 0x06, 0x11/0x12).
    Marked at LoadNativeEntry, at AddObject's positional
    follow-a-native rule, at EmitInstanceCallAOT, at the kImmediate128 split,
    and at GenerateTTSCall -- that last one inferred rather than disassembled,
    because it is fully inlined. 92 + 6 + 287 = their 385.

  * entries[].code is their copy of ObjectPool::DebugPrint with a
    "<N len string>" case added and "(raw)" renamed "(unknown)". The cutoff is
    measured in Utf8 bytes but the number printed is String::Length().

Measured against their own dump of their own base.so: pool size 1421 both
sides, `pairs` identical index for index, and 1323 of 1421 entry descriptions
identical. The 98 that differ are slots the deserializer rewrites to something
local to the analysing process.

op_dump_check.sh in the research tree is the standing check. Negative controls
(each with ninja exiting 0 in the same round): deduplicating the pp lists goes
red at 1459/1136; not preserving the mark across the switchable-call reset
takes `pairs` to 379; dropping GenerateTTSCall's marks takes it to 98; printing
Utf8::Length for long strings takes the identical entries to 1320.

verify_all.sh 16 ran / 0 failed, verify_reproduction.sh 28 artifacts / 0
failures, run_vm_tests 157 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

